      "lineNbr": 185,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-19T19:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(DSLExpression has a `type()` method already which exposes the expression\u0027s type, doesn\u0027t it?)\n\nThinking about this some more, maybe `IndexExpression::Convert` just needs to support \"type-ref+literal --\u003e array-type-reference\". At a glance I\u0027m not sure why this logic currently lives in `IRGenerator::convertIndexExpression`. Does it need anything IR generator-specific? Seems like that would make things cleaner all around.",
      "parentUuid": "cde54732_5d771726",
